    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d940">

                <pb facs="0847" n="840" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg840"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.93/423: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-28T09:00:00+08:00">December 28, 1937—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1238. Reference Department’s 697, December 27, 11 a.m.<anchor n="58"
                        xml:id="d940-f1"/> Allison and staff have sailed on the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Oahu</hi>. In paragraph 2 of my 1231, December 26, 6
                    p.m., I said that our officers were asked to postpone departure for Nanking
                    until after 1st of January. Japanese Consul General estimated it would require 3
                    or 4 days to proceed from Shanghai to Nanking and expected situation at Nanking
                    to be sufficiently cleared after about the 4th of January. Allison understands
                    this.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The <hi rendition="#italic">Oahu</hi> may visit Wuhu before proceeding to
                        Nanking. If so Allison will investigate the flag incident mentioned in my
                        No, 1219.<anchor n="59" xml:id="d940-f2"/></item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Allison has been supplied two gray codes and special gray cipher.
                            Espy<anchor n="60" xml:id="d940-f3"/> has the post’s consular rubber
                        stamp seal.</item>
                </list>
                <p>Repeated to Hankow and Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
